(laughing)

00:00:09.153 --> 00:00:12.350
(optimistic music)

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.183
Hey, legal eagles.

00:00:13.183 --> 00:00:15.440
It's time to think like a lawyer

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.990
or today it's time to laugh like a lawyer

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.670
because we're going to
have a change of pace,

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.400
and instead of destroying
your favorite childhood movie

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.740
or explaining why your
favorite legal drama

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.610
is completely full of holes,

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.440
Stella and I are going to
review some lawyer jokes.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.800
They're gonna make fun of me.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.873
Are you okay with that?

00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:33.706
(dog barks)

00:00:33.706 --> 00:00:34.760
So what I've done is I've asked a friend

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.960
to compile some lawyer jokes for me.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.430
I haven't seen these ahead of time.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.640
But let me know if you guys
like this change of format.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.370
And I've done enough stuff about PewDewPie

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.420
to know that meme review is a thing,

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.370
so let me know if you want me to respond

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.950
to legal or law school memes.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.410
I would love to make
this a continuing thing

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.280
because who are we if we
can't laugh at ourselves?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.543
Let's see if this is clean.

00:00:54.543 --> 00:00:55.630
(laughing)

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.639
Okay, but without further ado,

00:00:57.639 --> 00:01:01.203
let's dig into the first lawyer jokes.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.900
An attorney was working late one night

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.690
in his office when, suddenly,
Satan appeared before him.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:08.737
The devil made him an offer,

00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:10.137
"I will make it so you win every case

00:01:10.137 --> 00:01:12.067
"that you try for the rest of your life.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:14.237
"Your clients will worship
you, your colleagues will be

00:01:14.237 --> 00:01:16.957
"in awe and you will make
an enormous amount of money,

00:01:16.957 --> 00:01:19.017
"but in return you must give me your soul,

00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:20.677
"your wife's soul, the
souls of your children,

00:01:20.677 --> 00:01:21.907
"your parents, grandparents,

00:01:21.907 --> 00:01:24.150
"and those of all of your friends."

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.087
The lawyer thought about it
for a moment and then asked,

00:01:26.087 --> 00:01:27.820
"But what's the catch?"

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:28.720
(chuckling)

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.553
Oh god.

00:01:29.553 --> 00:01:30.980
We might not have souls,

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.128
but we care about the
souls of the loved ones

00:01:34.128 --> 00:01:35.700
that are in our lives.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.200
Also, by the way, it
wouldn't be unusual for Satan

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.463
to Apparate in front of
us, that happens everyday.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.020
What's the different between
a lawyer and a jellyfish?

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.610
One is a spineless, poisonous blob,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.292
the other is a form of sea life.

00:01:50.292 --> 00:01:51.125
(laughing)

00:01:51.125 --> 00:01:51.958
God.

00:01:51.958 --> 00:01:53.730
I would say that most of
the lawyers that I know

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.470
are actually very courageous

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.110
and are willing to work very,
very hard for their clients.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.750
Why would a lawyer be spineless?

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.383
I mean, poisonous, okay sure.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.490
A 50 year-old lawyer
who has been practicing

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:10.010
since he was 25 passed away and arrived

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:11.550
at the pearly gates for judgment.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.017
The lawyer said to Saint Peter,

00:02:13.017 --> 00:02:14.277
"There must be some mistake.

00:02:14.277 --> 00:02:17.760
"I'm only 50 years old and
that's far too young to die."

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.897
Saint Peter frowned
and consulted his book,

00:02:19.897 --> 00:02:20.730
"That's funny.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.017
"When we added up all
your billing records,

00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:24.096
"you should be at least 83 by now."

00:02:24.096 --> 00:02:25.320
(laughing)

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.420
I like that one.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.330
This one hits close to home

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.370
because there are some lawyers out there

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:33.600
who are unethical and they will bill

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.960
their client for more work
than they've actually done

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.960
and this is reasonably ethical
where you're on a plane

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.860
and because of the shift in timezones,

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.610
you're actually able to
build more than 24 hours

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.770
in the entire day

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.820
if you were literally working
every single hour of the day.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:55.310
So you were up all night,
you did an all-nighter

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.490
and then you flew backwards

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.080
from the east coast to west coast.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.750
It is conceivably possible
and there are some rockstar

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.260
associates who have been known to do that,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.413
but yeah, fair point.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:08.763
Oh god.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:10.900
Let's see if this is clean.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.020
Why does the Bar Association
Code of Ethics prevent

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.320
sex between lawyers and their clients?

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.240
To prevent clients from being billed twice

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.100
for essentially the same service.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.600
Hopefully you have a better experience

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.690
than, we'll say, getting
screwed by your attorney.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.830
Actually California just
changed their ethics rules.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.810
It used to be that in
California you could engage

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.570
in a romantic relationship
with your client

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:37.130
and now, at least during the
pendency of your relationship

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.870
is unethical in California

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:41.090
to have that relationship
with your client.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.370
So, realistically speaking,

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.600
you can get in big trouble in California.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.083
Yeah, that's a big change.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.360
At a convention of biological scientists,

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.957
one researcher remarks to another,

00:03:50.957 --> 00:03:52.377
"Did you know that in our lab

00:03:52.377 --> 00:03:56.037
"we have switched from mice to
lawyers for our experiments?"

00:03:56.037 --> 00:03:57.097
"Really?" the other replied.

00:03:57.097 --> 00:03:58.217
"Why did you switch?"

00:03:58.217 --> 00:03:59.597
"Well, for three reasons."

00:03:59.597 --> 00:04:02.377
"First we found that lawyers
are far more plentiful.

00:04:02.377 --> 00:04:05.097
"Second, the lab assistants
don't get so attached to them,

00:04:05.097 --> 00:04:08.430
"and thirdly there some
things even a rat won't do."

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.750
(laughing)

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:10.583
Oh god.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:14.220
But, frankly, if you hire
a lawyer and you need them

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.300
to help you on your case,
you're gonna want them

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.270
to be flexible and to
be a zealous advocate

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.630
and to really get in the trenches

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.630
with the rest of the rats, oh my god.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.873
Lawyers are far more
expensive than rats, though.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.660
Why did New Jersey get all the toxic waste

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.910
and California get all the lawyers?

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.722
New Jersey got first pick.

00:04:33.722 --> 00:04:35.100
All right, fair enough.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.860
The California legal market is huge.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.440
That's where I have practiced
for most of my career.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.410
Frankly, I prefer
California than New Jersey.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:43.883
So suck it, New Jersey.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.330
Two physicians boarded
a flight out of Seattle.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.570
One sat in the window seat,

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:50.770
the other sat in the middle seat.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.910
Just before takeoff, an attorney got on

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:55.700
and took the aisle seat
next to the two physicians.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.020
The attorney kicked off his shoes,

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.450
wiggled his toes and was
setting in when the physician

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.737
in the window seat said,

00:05:00.737 --> 00:05:02.607
"I think I'll get up and get a coke."

00:05:02.607 --> 00:05:03.617
"No problem", said the attorney.

00:05:03.617 --> 00:05:04.850
"I'll get it for you."

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.570
When he was done one of
the physicians picked up

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.250
the attorney's shoe and spat in it.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.147
When he returned with the
coke, the physician said,

00:05:10.147 --> 00:05:12.090
"That looks good, I
think I'll have one too."

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.030
Again, the attorney
obligingly went to fetch it

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.220
and while he was gone,

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.990
the other physician picked up
the other shoe and spat in it.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:18.860
The attorney returned

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.850
and they all sat back
and enjoyed the flight.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:21.850
As the plane was landing,

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:23.820
the attorney slipped
his feet into his shoes

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.907
and knew immediately what had happened.

00:05:25.907 --> 00:05:28.177
"How long must this go on?" he asked.

00:05:28.177 --> 00:05:29.767
"This fighting between our professions,

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:31.257
"this hatred, this animosity,

00:05:31.257 --> 00:05:34.041
"this spitting in shoes
and pissing in cokes?"

00:05:34.041 --> 00:05:35.462
(laughing)

00:05:35.462 --> 00:05:37.150
So I have a lot of doctor friends.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:37.983
I don't think there's

00:05:37.983 --> 00:05:42.850
much animosity between
lawyers and doctors.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.240
Really it's just between
me and Doctor Mike

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.950
because we've never done a collaboration.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.540
You know what you've done, Doctor Mike.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.160
- Dude, you're hilarious and if you ever

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.403
wanna make a YouTube video, I'm so down.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.150
- A lawyer was filling
out a job application

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:58.840
when he came to the question
have you ever been arrested?

00:05:58.840 --> 00:05:59.673
He answered no.

00:05:59.673 --> 00:06:01.450
Next question, intended for applications

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.820
who had answered yes was why?

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.285
The lawyer answered
it, "Never got caught."

00:06:06.285 --> 00:06:07.940
(laughing)

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.830
So the thing is it's
really the rare exception

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.690
that it's like a Bernie Madoff

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:16.070
or some other corporate raider

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.790
who has done some illegal act.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:20.132
That and the doctors,
they're the real criminals.

00:06:20.132 --> 00:06:21.213
♪ Bye, bye, bye ♪

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:22.051
♪ Bye, bye, bye ♪

00:06:22.051 --> 00:06:23.134
- C'mon, son!

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:27.030
- A secretary, a paralegal, and a partner

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.250
in a city law firm are
walking through a park

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.390
on their way to lunch when
they find an antique oil lamp.

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.880
They rub it and a genie
appears out of a puff of smoke.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.897
The genie says, "I only
grant three wishes,

00:06:36.897 --> 00:06:38.647
"so I'll give each of you just one."

00:06:38.647 --> 00:06:40.307
"Me first, me first," says the secretary.

00:06:40.307 --> 00:06:42.287
"I want to be in the
Bahamas driving a speedboat

00:06:42.287 --> 00:06:43.440
"without a care in the world."

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.307
Poof, she's gone.

00:06:44.307 --> 00:06:46.387
"Me next, me next," says the paralegal.

00:06:46.387 --> 00:06:48.577
"I want to be in Hawaii
relaxing on the beach

00:06:48.577 --> 00:06:50.687
"with my personal masseuse
and an endless supply

00:06:50.687 --> 00:06:52.980
"of pina coladas and the love of my life."

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.077
Poof, he's gone.

00:06:54.077 --> 00:06:56.310
"You're next." The genie
says to the partner.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.917
The partner says, "I want those two back

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.788
"in the office after lunch."

00:06:59.788 --> 00:07:00.930
(laughing)

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.360
There's definitely some truth to that.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:05.830
I have had some great luck in my career

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:09.254
to have some fantastic legal
secretaries and paralegals

00:07:09.254 --> 00:07:12.670
in my office and they have saved my bacon

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.370
on more than one occasion.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.493
Man, you're not getting away that easily.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.250
All right, let's see, this
one is in the first person.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.900
I was in juvenile court
prosecuting a teen suspected

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.860
of burglary when the judge
asked everyone to stand

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:29.427
and state his or her name and
role for the court reporter.

00:07:29.427 --> 00:07:31.747
"Leah Rauch, deputy prosecutor," I said.

00:07:31.747 --> 00:07:33.710
"Linda Jones, probation officer."

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.637
'Sam Clark, public defender."

00:07:35.637 --> 00:07:37.897
"John," said the teen who was on trial.

00:07:37.897 --> 00:07:40.038
"I'm the one who stole the truck.

00:07:40.038 --> 00:07:42.430
(laughing)

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:43.759
Okay, yeah.

00:07:43.759 --> 00:07:44.592
(exhales)

00:07:44.592 --> 00:07:46.320
That one hits close to home.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.080
If only I could control
what my clients said

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.100
at all times because they have a habit

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.184
of saying the worst possible thing

00:07:53.184 --> 00:07:55.070
at the worst possible time.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.080
It's a mark of a good lawyer

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:59.223
when you can control a very bad witness.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.820
When my 88 year-old mother was called

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:04.410
for jury duty she had to submit

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:06.340
to questioning by the opposing lawyers.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:07.257
That's called voir dire.

00:08:07.257 --> 00:08:08.880
"Have you ever dealt with an attorney?"

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.257
Asked the plaintiff's lawyer.

00:08:10.257 --> 00:08:12.560
"Yes, I had an attorney
write my living trust,"

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.787
she responded.

00:08:13.787 --> 00:08:14.917
"How did that turn out?"

00:08:14.917 --> 00:08:15.987
"I don't know," she said.

00:08:15.987 --> 00:08:17.995
"Ask me when I'm dead.

00:08:17.995 --> 00:08:19.160
(laughing)

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.580
Ah, some good old fashioned
the states and trusts humor.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:23.653
That's always great.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.410
All right last one, here we go.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:28.243
What's the difference

00:08:28.243 --> 00:08:29.770
between a good lawyer and a bad lawyer?

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:32.810
A bad lawyer might let a case
drag on for several years.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:36.030
A good lawyer knows how to
make it last even longer.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.900
Too mean, too mean.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:40.300
Oh, where those good?

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.740
Where those good lawyer jokes?

